# Prepared document runtime implementation plan

Type: Implementation Plan
Date: October 24, 2026
Status: Accepted direction; implementation pending
Architecture authority: [prepared-document-runtime.acd](../acd/prepared-document-runtime.acd)
Implementation branch: `codex/prepared-document-runtime` (not created by documentation cleanup)

## Goal and constraints

Prepare a versioned instrumented document with character voice bindings and resident synthesis resources, keeping heavy work off the UI and ordinary character transitions continuous. Preserve existing normalized models, implemented startup warmup and follower coalescing. One branch and one PR cover this plan. No neural provider is selected.

## Dependencies

A runnable native Flutter/Dart toolchain, compatible pinned Kokoro assets, and measurable native cleanup behavior. The current ignored SDK contains an Intel Dart executable that this Apple Silicon execution environment cannot run. Investigate before changing the dependency baseline.

## [ ] P0 — Establish baseline and failure fixtures

Depends on: none.
Scope: verify toolchain; run focused import, attribution, runtime and playback tests; record startup warmup, A/B/A routes, native sessions/tensors and memory. Confirm startup already uses 8s target, 4s/two-chunk acceptance and a 5s timeout; these are not missing features.
Validation: reproducible native baseline plus controlled delayed-worker/startup-selection tests. Evidence belongs in the completion record; no success is inferred from existing test files.
Completion evidence: pending.

## [ ] P1 — Prepared document revision owner

Depends on: P0.
Scope: move parsing/normalization/analysis and serialization behind a document preparation supervisor; coalesce source changes and reject stale success/failure/cleanup; distinguish display readiness from speech readiness.
Validation: long-document UI responsiveness, overlapping reload and cancellation tests, artifact fidelity.
Completion evidence: pending.

## [ ] P2 — Character bindings and resident runtime resources

Depends on: P0, P1.
Scope: retain current character identity/evidence data; add versioned voice/model references and validation; reuse a long-lived worker/model and loaded voice vectors; release inference tensors and drain/close resources safely. Address the documented macOS close workaround with native evidence.
Validation: hundreds of uncached A/B/A chunks, bounded resources, timeout/exit/shutdown cases, corrupted asset handling.
Completion evidence: pending.

## [ ] P3 — Worker-owned planning and buffer policy

Depends on: P1, P2.
Scope: move controller realization/planning and CPU-heavy boundary/export work to explicit owners. Refine existing lead scheduling into bounded contiguous lookahead with measured startup/refill policy; preserve native append-only forward queue behavior and follower coalescing.
Validation: missing predecessor, slow renderer, short document, active export competition and actual UI/audio continuity.
Completion evidence: pending.

## [ ] P4 — Assignment revisions and cache provenance

Depends on: P2, P3.
Scope: derive cache fingerprints from bindings and effective realization; atomic publication. Prepare replacement future audio for assignment edits and commit only at a safe boundary. Newest revision wins before first audio. Do not introduce automatic cache eviction without a separate approved retention decision.
Validation: full-buffer edits, A/B/C startup edits, stale events, same voice id with changed bytes, queued-file retention.
Completion evidence: pending.

## [ ] FINAL — Validate, reconcile and archive

Depends on: P0–P4.
Scope: run the [integrated scenarios](../test-specifications/prepared-document-and-buffered-playback.md); reconcile implemented facts into affected architecture; update setup/use/troubleshooting under docs; remove superseded target contracts; archive this plan and ACD together; prepare one PR.
Validation: native/audio evidence, responsiveness and bounded resources; documentation checks; explicit docs-impact record. Do not archive with blocked acceptance.
Completion evidence: pending.
